notes:
At the start of this session the module was already built on the branch. Its first run_tests passed all 29 tests (test_MOD031 21/21, test_MOD031_dev 8/8). The roundtrip of MIG-0033 passes, and check passes; the sqlfluff findings are advisory, mostly the lower-case style of the Phase 1 files, which was kept.

What was built:
- Through change scripts, local_group_id, contact_country_id and contact_region are added to the tables in the plan, and the grain keys are widened (the fact's unique clustered index now has ten columns).
- Existing rows get placeholder values: local_group_id 0, contact_country_id = country_id, contact_region = region. Adjustment rows written before deployment get local_group_id -2.
- The migration empties the five snapshot tables and writes the 'local_group_restatement' marker. While the marker is there, the daily count takes the full path. It records only real changes, at the own-country grain with local_group_id -2. Where MOD-028's marker is also present, it uses -2 in the segment columns too, and one run removes both markers.
- Gold country_id is the list's dim_country_id for a reportable local group, and otherwise the silver country.
- A region longer than varchar(12) fails usp_load_silv_member_state_ranges with error 50031, naming the whole value. It is never cut short, and nothing is written.

The dev tests cover:
- country 0 with and without a usable group;
- a contact with no live contact row;
- a profile update when only the local group changed;
- gold for a group that is no longer reportable;
- the log counts for a group move on the normal path;
- a change to the own-country region alone, which stays on the normal path;
- the detail as-known-at function on the new columns;
- the error path for a region that is too long.

No grants (DES-001: MOD-031 adds none).

Test-first: the first run had 21 of 21 of the Tester's tests passing; the final run passed 21 of 21 and 8 unit test(s), in 1 run(s).
